            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0747" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.156 CH/240: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-07T16:00:00+09:00">October 7, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 8—7:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>650. Department’s 338, September 28, 6 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d799-f1"/>
                    Chefoo Harbor Commission. Formal note was delivered today to the Foreign Office.
                    The British Ambassador has taken similar action.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking and Chefoo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
